#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100725 :question/id #uuid "e092e191-84ac-5d9f-b0db-94d628a6154e" :question/math-academy-id "e-525" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny' = -\\dfrac{y}{x}, \\qquad x \\neq 0\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f'(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$\n\n- Substituting $y = f(x)$ and $y' = f'(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement\n\n- The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Differentiating $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Substituting $y = \\dfrac{1}{x}$ and $y' = -\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{y}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & \\overset{?}{=}-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}{x} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the function $y = \\dfrac{1}{x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100795 :question/id #uuid "f5ffa549-e77e-5db4-9fde-5b0134957539" :question/math-academy-id "e-8732" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{3y}{x}, \\qquad y(-1) = -2.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y = Ax^3$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y = Ax^3$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1) = -2.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y({\\color{red}{-1}}) = {\\color{blue}{-2}}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{3} \\\\ -2 & =A(-1)^{3} \\\\ -2 & =A(-1) \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = 2x^3 .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100801 :question/id #uuid "1228900d-87d4-5ff0-8e01-ff9417e82220" :question/math-academy-id "e-9978" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y = e^x + 1$\n\n- $y = -e^x$\n\n- $y = 2e^x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y = e^x + 1,$ we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = e^x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ {e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}{e}^{x}+1 \\\\ 0 & \\ne 1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *false*. Therefore, the function $y = e^x+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y = -e^x,$ we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = -e^x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ -{e}^{x} & =-{e}^{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y = -e^x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y = 2e^x,$ we get $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = 2e^x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ 2{e}^{x} & =2{e}^{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y = 2e^x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101155 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8245f03-8a88-51b1-816d-b194c8191459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437920} {:answer/id #uuid "241c8aac-057f-5bd8-8672-538887a90f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8245f03-8a88-51b1-816d-b194c8191459" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8022058-91f7-5a21-86f8-cda411ec1bea" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{5}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95795348-591c-5f80-a9dc-9d6695fa2629" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437922} {:answer/id #uuid "e733e51a-85ca-5ec8-b45a-8579524491ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e733e51a-85ca-5ec8-b45a-8579524491ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437923} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8576006-7ef6-5181-a3ea-35a1c7c390e2" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f72c83c-eb8c-5631-b3a6-b174e90aab92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437924} {:answer/id #uuid "589c074c-f210-5e65-911b-aa087fdb7ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "589c074c-f210-5e65-911b-aa087fdb7ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437925} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e1d7437-eee9-54ee-a6bc-2720730fc72d" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b2e480d-7f17-59ba-a02c-a786007bf39b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140631" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)={x}^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=5{x}^{5}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)={x}^{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3} \\\\  & \\ne 5{x}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y={x}^{4}$ and ${y}^{′}=4{x}^{3}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4y}{x} \\\\ (4{x}^{3}) & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4({x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 4{x}^{3} & =4{x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y={x}^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5b5d65b-ec6c-51b7-9cdd-88d75d5264d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098272} {:answer/id #uuid "120fac45-9287-5ac3-9100-a665688ad407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098273} {:answer/id #uuid "2b917d15-1467-52ba-b80f-ce6601b19575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098274} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc1975e-b88f-59af-b700-be8515c0465a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098275} {:answer/id #uuid "43c462fc-7958-5b11-abe9-5c053ed82ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098276}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f720a1-e094-53ee-b045-f9df2b9d62de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098271}] :question/id #uuid "42bb61a9-d18d-5d5b-88a0-be6dbf1c9579" :question/math-academy-id "q-141055" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx} = 2y, y(1) = 3.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y = Ae^{2x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101157 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df433686-7b08-5422-9159-68e30b1dd3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437926} {:answer/id #uuid "be8d3f83-dbd7-5512-8e52-cbb77918ee9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be8d3f83-dbd7-5512-8e52-cbb77918ee9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437927} :answer-field/id #uuid "3da2476a-cd94-5d52-b20c-ba45588a2e94" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438992} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "697f7e93-3daf-5d09-aaa0-33a0a696b34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437928} {:answer/id #uuid "66aac766-51f7-5829-b96d-8fdbe93a04eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66aac766-51f7-5829-b96d-8fdbe93a04eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437929} :answer-field/id #uuid "13228480-d8e3-59b9-a952-c0a713529199" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438993} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bbf35f7-eca9-5cd8-a4bb-3916780464ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437930} {:answer/id #uuid "e90e9605-ee1b-56aa-a246-8f89f26d5c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e90e9605-ee1b-56aa-a246-8f89f26d5c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437931} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4b74fc-fbff-523b-9711-9570469a2063" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "47b66471-b70f-5509-8368-6a6674b74447" :question/math-academy-id "q-141078" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)={e}^{2x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)={e}^{2x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{2x})}^{′} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}^{′}=2{e}^{2x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ 2{e}^{2x} & =2{e}^{2x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${f}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101158 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10dd2375-3309-5242-9f4a-93a4d27c3816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437992} {:answer/id #uuid "b369a12e-1a9e-53c9-a28e-7de7d2f0dd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b369a12e-1a9e-53c9-a28e-7de7d2f0dd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437993} :answer-field/id #uuid "f260d360-832c-5eaf-a407-8777898370d7" :answer-field/key "$y=-2{e}^{-2x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b2ec8c3-2e15-5684-9c02-a21fd6230b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437994} {:answer/id #uuid "44b02a34-b812-5969-824c-b1a36338dbbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b2ec8c3-2e15-5684-9c02-a21fd6230b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437994} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8de5f6f-2c45-581c-b864-deb370031b0b" :answer-field/key "$y=-2{e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a8b9c15-73b7-50fd-80af-8ff120fa6ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437996} {:answer/id #uuid "977a699e-8cdd-54d7-b2cb-49b49d93ef59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437997}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a8b9c15-73b7-50fd-80af-8ff120fa6ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437996} :answer-field/id #uuid "f011be38-b8ff-5f20-b55b-d93017ba44c0" :answer-field/key "$y=2{e}^{-x}+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439027} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed2e962f-0c82-5252-b1c3-52a6cbdc5517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667964} {:answer/id #uuid "6e62fe59-b153-55ef-be33-20f23f86246e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed2e962f-0c82-5252-b1c3-52a6cbdc5517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667964} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea31cb84-3391-51fb-8fe2-69c560164572" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668259}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e22d897d-f7ce-5b4f-b6d4-aa4c45c66b5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141096" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{-2x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{-2x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{-2x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{-2x} & =4{e}^{-2x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(-2{e}^{x}) \\\\ -2{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 6{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=-2{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2{e}^{-x}+1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2{e}^{-x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2y \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-2(2{e}^{-x}+1) \\\\ -2{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-4{e}^{-x}-2 \\\\ 2{e}^{-x} & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2{e}^{-x}+1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=-2{e}^{-2x}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8968d782-5c74-5e7b-b779-8cbfc2e7b716" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098290} {:answer/id #uuid "8cdf33b5-c72f-51a0-b0ca-dbf427183cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098291} {:answer/id #uuid "94b06eab-3c8d-5854-9e4c-da8f5d45c63a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098292} {:answer/id #uuid "984c5e03-478d-5b00-b114-3fbe4f6f1cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098293} {:answer/id #uuid "4c69d0cf-6289-5358-a8d6-b7b5d72161aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098294}] :answer-field/id #uuid "386faf29-f883-5197-a57f-f605f304e704" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098289}] :question/id #uuid "50fb0b0b-198a-530e-b586-9313a3c7912c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141117" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx} = y^{2}, y(1) = 4.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y = \\frac{1}{A - x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "babc8bec-aec4-50b2-983c-a5c5e19babf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438580} {:answer/id #uuid "0e681d75-6b90-5dfe-a3b1-fa927459e41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e681d75-6b90-5dfe-a3b1-fa927459e41a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438581} :answer-field/id #uuid "008e9eb2-6761-57ab-9978-fe105459b52b" :answer-field/key "$y=2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276e25b7-9187-5abb-9fa1-e532f9e988be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438582} {:answer/id #uuid "d44e3b64-6a02-5556-acfb-ebac7d16150e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276e25b7-9187-5abb-9fa1-e532f9e988be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438582} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b80ace-4085-5ca5-b15f-49cdc840fdc8" :answer-field/key "$y={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9303d64-f302-585f-918a-f75cda94e15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438584} {:answer/id #uuid "1db5d556-052a-51c4-994e-edad39635f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9303d64-f302-585f-918a-f75cda94e15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438584} :answer-field/id #uuid "997a3d7e-abcd-5f9a-bdb1-6ad87c83170f" :answer-field/key "$y={x}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a773fc2b-812d-5f5c-8cbb-9b1672c48928" :question/math-academy-id "q-79335" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2y}{x}-2,\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot 2x}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{x}-2 \\\\ 2 & \\overset{?}{=}4-2 \\\\ 2 & =2.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=2x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{2},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot {x}^{2}}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x}-2 \\\\ 2x & \\overset{?}{=}2x-2 \\\\ 0 & \\ne -2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *false*. Therefore, the function $y={x}^{2}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{3},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2y}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2\\cdot {x}^{3}}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{x}-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & \\overset{?}{=}2{x}^{2}-2 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ne -2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{3}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=2x$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} {:answer/id #uuid "7c777b71-5609-57b6-98cd-5de6ad97f13e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cf84e4-bf37-53ee-9c4e-c48312865eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437932} :answer-field/id #uuid "1754ff84-62e2-5fa6-b4ab-1a4ed225ccf5" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438995} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd869c55-39da-53e6-ae83-c00f9f75727e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437934} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebf7563-afa0-50f3-97cb-0e17f76f6a4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd869c55-39da-53e6-ae83-c00f9f75727e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437934} :answer-field/id #uuid "94674f44-214d-51de-8806-6b7b3a2c49aa" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438996} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68878cd7-dc72-5e55-800f-d9aceba0d493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437936} {:answer/id #uuid "5695c90a-25d5-5c15-8845-780cd00f9341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68878cd7-dc72-5e55-800f-d9aceba0d493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437936} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41c643e-8038-5852-a780-537545979885" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438997} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab9c8bc6-905e-5dde-a9bf-2d4212c4f0ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668385} {:answer/id #uuid "0e5f8ce3-6b39-5fa1-bbd9-900501dad42d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e5f8ce3-6b39-5fa1-bbd9-900501dad42d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668386} :answer-field/id #uuid "096d33ab-16cd-57de-a4b5-bbc0274aa5cd" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c28aa3d-73cf-552e-9e05-dfc5bcb67151" :question/math-academy-id "q-141080" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2y\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\  & \\ne 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}2y \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x & \\ne \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc440dfb-329e-5cce-98e2-d61a73c6573b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437938} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3e6505-7161-5f6a-be56-c236d5b1a400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb3e6505-7161-5f6a-be56-c236d5b1a400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437939} :answer-field/id #uuid "062dd2dc-b6ff-50a1-9e87-20f44d397210" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438998} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97fcaffe-490b-50d3-bd81-11d7998b6387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437940} {:answer/id #uuid "bfde07d3-eb9e-55be-b75d-2f6e35461ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97fcaffe-490b-50d3-bd81-11d7998b6387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437940} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e330e7c-b25a-5b7f-9f95-b68a2feb22aa" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438999} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60c19038-4ad6-599a-bc53-f97ce9ff756a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437942} {:answer/id #uuid "22a53b8b-e4ab-51f5-a137-7c3a442b5a2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60c19038-4ad6-599a-bc53-f97ce9ff756a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437942} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad20673a-9803-59bc-b2e5-d66a0d3efe10" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "82065c87-2fb6-51b8-8d32-9c57d0719fb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141081" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ and ${y}^{′}=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x & \\ne {cos}^{2}⁡2x\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${f}^{′}(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76321bcd-1dfe-54f5-8624-a1897a3eb02d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437944} {:answer/id #uuid "74e24dca-87ac-5021-88ea-6d2cad76cfe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e24dca-87ac-5021-88ea-6d2cad76cfe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437945} :answer-field/id #uuid "96ed6203-45be-5de5-bbe2-94c88e917af6" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439001} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83ec8f2a-644e-5350-a178-f851274405b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437946} {:answer/id #uuid "f48e3736-83c7-5b2f-8b2a-b7622b40ed4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48e3736-83c7-5b2f-8b2a-b7622b40ed4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437947} :answer-field/id #uuid "9225aa09-89ea-55c4-8ca6-de93ab83d375" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439002} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67767ab0-4e77-5125-a2ab-a6302dab16e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437948} {:answer/id #uuid "adffa49b-1f3c-5361-8969-94df35c322c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adffa49b-1f3c-5361-8969-94df35c322c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437949} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd1164d-c8c5-54ab-8801-2a7ea56a251e" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9b7a88f7-a074-5f69-9224-f1585f849cc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-141082" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{y}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9eb1ace-da7e-5399-a3fe-3eca3341dc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437950} {:answer/id #uuid "8294de83-bfe6-5d3e-907f-46fca51b308f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9eb1ace-da7e-5399-a3fe-3eca3341dc04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437950} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f826ec9-1240-515d-9e72-2dd14068a0b0" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "307652cb-8dec-5139-b1b9-8b42d2c243ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437952} {:answer/id #uuid "d0fc6fa1-75d1-54ae-a895-4bd473e2976a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "307652cb-8dec-5139-b1b9-8b42d2c243ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437952} :answer-field/id #uuid "93d26810-7687-5dab-8301-97c0074dc993" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "430fce2c-320b-5e26-93df-7d20527603a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437954} {:answer/id #uuid "4dee6609-1868-55be-9c34-9e4174a83b33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "430fce2c-320b-5e26-93df-7d20527603a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437954} :answer-field/id #uuid "81855480-1021-5030-8cb7-a5a2db6e6e14" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d055e430-5e3a-5949-a626-8f28d9d6bd4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668387} {:answer/id #uuid "721989e3-46c2-58b7-b5c9-50db24749e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "721989e3-46c2-58b7-b5c9-50db24749e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668388} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6d61de9-f6fe-5e89-834f-fb296e0eb905" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c4402732-29b4-541b-a6e6-a372fd33bf97" :question/math-academy-id "q-141084" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={\\left(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & \\ne -\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{\\left(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\right)}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} & \\ne -\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "654fa534-773a-593f-977c-52c967bc6758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437956} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1670b2-e9d2-5154-a206-4f8b1150ce6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "654fa534-773a-593f-977c-52c967bc6758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437956} :answer-field/id #uuid "3757fe80-c2f2-5c86-bda7-b8b1794c555f" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{-x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7283afb-092e-5737-a0c8-37560698d7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437958} {:answer/id #uuid "23367094-d892-5aa7-a778-191ce481dae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7283afb-092e-5737-a0c8-37560698d7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437958} :answer-field/id #uuid "517f6faa-1205-51b0-a3ed-acee4119eb37" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80cf2045-8273-57f1-bbce-39810be44be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437960} {:answer/id #uuid "814d7525-ee34-5bf5-a23b-7ddd661f2801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80cf2045-8273-57f1-bbce-39810be44be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437960} :answer-field/id #uuid "da8265e0-a0fc-5f6a-becf-ca88b952fcad" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f912e19-4101-5137-ae0c-984ae5d69931" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668389} {:answer/id #uuid "382cb1de-87f4-599f-97cb-31c6481d52ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382cb1de-87f4-599f-97cb-31c6481d52ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668390} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf9e9cee-1b46-506a-be30-74cabfe2478a" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "33a5a8c7-40f0-5353-a590-88087e77753a" :question/math-academy-id "q-141086" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-3y\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=3{e}^{-x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{-x}$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=3{e}^{-x},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(3{e}^{-x})}^{′} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-x} \\\\  & \\ne 3{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=3{e}^{-x}$ and ${y}^{′}=-3{e}^{-x}$ into the original equation, we get a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}-3y \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\overset{?}{=}-3(3{e}^{-x}) \\\\ -3{e}^{-x} & \\ne -9{e}^{-x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=3{e}^{-x}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce779982-5956-53ce-8f93-98847edcb147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437962} {:answer/id #uuid "20333a47-4e71-5ec5-9d41-91782cb4b909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce779982-5956-53ce-8f93-98847edcb147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437962} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cefe8de-ad3c-5341-b5a8-44e7ce7436d0" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4113f3b5-d089-56b5-ba2d-bdb03486c6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437964} {:answer/id #uuid "1edc75ea-b6e2-5bab-aebd-7ef159ff5c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1edc75ea-b6e2-5bab-aebd-7ef159ff5c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437965} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1cc3bda-6bd3-5d8e-bcf2-7853efc526c4" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439011} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ca0f560-582b-5ed2-ae44-d30f3b653470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437966} {:answer/id #uuid "0a6fcbcf-baa0-52ca-98cd-0ff0fd8d97f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6fcbcf-baa0-52ca-98cd-0ff0fd8d97f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437967} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f1c7da-9254-5126-a28b-3e9af246aaa4" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c072557-1ef3-577b-ad62-6b56bbe3d39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668391} {:answer/id #uuid "dfdf4d63-e493-5c11-82b2-2c221e258c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c072557-1ef3-577b-ad62-6b56bbe3d39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668391} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6da847b-12dc-5ace-b240-977bc91f758c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9c8904e1-5f17-5951-8dbc-61b76cd0babc" :question/math-academy-id "q-141088" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4x}{{e}^{y/2}}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{4x}$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x} \\\\  & \\ne \\frac{1}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and ${y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{x}$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{y/2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)/2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{x} & =\\frac{4}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3562e5cf-f895-5f46-86d8-1f4d377e852c" :answer/type {:db/id 