\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${f}^{′}(x)=-7x$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=-5{x}^{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-5{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-5\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-10x \\\\  & \\ne -7x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=-5{x}^{2}$ and ${y}^{′}=-10x$ into the original equation, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ -10x & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2(-5{x}^{2})}{x} \\\\ -10x & =-10x\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=-5{x}^{2}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and ${y}^{′}={f}^{′}(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494099 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011418b9-1534-59df-abe2-f6a8f8a26db8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494074} {:answer/id #uuid "021de50f-ea33-579e-a44c-452e1f743ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021de50f-ea33-579e-a44c-452e1f743ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494075} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4d4fa50-0013-5de3-852e-7f4ee29ad547" :answer-field/key "${f}^{′}(x)=-6{x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/ch