17592186494179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54e193b0-efba-5f1d-9e44-cf90148ec585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494163} :answer-field/id #uuid "de72884f-8c58-5c74-aa9c-e35bf2e4d062" :answer-field/key "$y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ed22e244-8467-5b30-9a78-06a03f1761ac" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}},\\,x>0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{3}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)},$ we get $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x}.\n$$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\left(3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{3}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{0}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{3}{x} & =\\frac{3}{x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1,$ we get $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\left(2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3e^{\\frac{1}{3}}\\cdot e^{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}}\\right)} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3 e^{\\frac{1}{3}}}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{x} - \\frac{3 e^{\\frac{1}{3}}}{x^{\\frac{2}{3}}} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=3 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494220 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3db4e6c-ec76-5c68-b9ea-8a870249452d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494208} {:answer/id #uuid "eedafe67-a61c-5e88-8cb0-53e032a87451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3db4e6c-ec76-5c68-b9ea-8a870249452d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494208} :answer-field/id #uuid "3621bd74-a8f3-532e-93ba-8265ce22c897" :answer-field/key "$y=- 3 e^{x} - 2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494148} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "807d73f1-95c3-5598-b78d-c5c37b01ff37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494177} {:answer/id #uuid "f380cb57-bb9a-55b5-8bb7-5942f0098316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f380cb57-bb9a-55b5-8bb7-5942f0098316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494221} :answer-field/id #uuid "c64eae15-0d0b-5d44-aa93-8afc1cfa5199" :answer-field/key "$y=- 2 e^{- x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52571d72-0344-521b-acf7-3b8804ca0284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494162} {:answer/id #uuid "67f09018-86bc-53cd-a196-213802abc706" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52571d72-0344-521b-acf7-3b8804ca0284" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494162} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcf53b2e-9588-5276-aeec-2aee943daafe" :answer-field/key "$y=3 e^{x} + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f13e106a-779d-594b-9ac2-fa322d45064e" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=3 e^{x} + 1,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(3 e^{x} + 1\\right) \\\\ 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}3 e^{x} + 1 \\\\ -1 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=3 e^{x} + 1$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 2 e^{- x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 e^{- x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ 2 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- 2 e^{- x}\\right) \\\\ 2 e^{- x} & \\overset{?}{=}- 2 e^{- x} \\\\ 4 e^{- x} & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 2 e^{- x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- 3 e^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ - 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}1\\cdot \\left(- 3 e^{x} - 2\\right) \\\\ - 3 e^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}- 3 e^{x} - 2 \\\\ 2 & \\not\\equiv 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=- 3 e^{x} - 2$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b697512-d6ce-5d58-bc2f-44300a470396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577184} {:answer/id #uuid "4421f52c-8db7-510c-a3d0-e08d93874bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b697512-d6ce-5d58-bc2f-44300a470396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577184} :answer-field/id #uuid "3495b22a-5a40-5f4c-a29c-2521e744ca38" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eb60bde-94b4-5458-b7f4-9d69e214bb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577185} {:answer/id #uuid "a93e1b70-b465-590a-b650-b80a76b041e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a93e1b70-b465-590a-b650-b80a76b041e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577213} :answer-field/id #uuid "70375abd-6d28-58de-b77f-ce69697a327a" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f2b71f-67b4-5220-b1f2-f9c9f3e2990b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577179} {:answer/id #uuid "66b843bb-147d-5696-b9c6-20fb6aa9e3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66b843bb-147d-5696-b9c6-20fb6aa9e3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577203} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce88c0d7-692b-5115-9ff0-7a3fad5b60fe" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{5}{3 x}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "45c5715f-9b0f-5612-a118-607bd8abc3ff" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=3 e^{- y},\\qquad 3 x>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{5}{3 x}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{3 x}\\cdot 3 \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{5}{3 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}3 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{3}{e^{\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(3 x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e396c4fd-71c1-59bc-9209-55e931510240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577222} {:answer/id #uuid "e6df26ad-bd81-5aaa-81e2-ef34d75cdbe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6df26ad-bd81-5aaa-81e2-ef34d75cdbe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577224} :answer-field/id #uuid "6808e726-3826-52a1-816d-23e80ef6d446" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577204} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c7a9207-df6c-50b8-9322-193b412462e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577197} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e176ae-2161-5a2f-98fa-6518aaefb7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c7a9207-df6c-50b8-9322-193b412462e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577197} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b09d08b-9296-54a5-9074-0d5f596c8957" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f89bbee-f608-509b-809c-754a660a177f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577200} {:answer/id #uuid "93c10b1d-09b9-596a-91ee-b34e3f0aeb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577212}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93c10b1d-09b9-596a-91ee-b34e3f0aeb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577212} :answer-field/id #uuid "b30d6233-d2d5-5248-b659-81906ac6d588" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "628c5962-9540-54e0-a743-71b039507ef9" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=2 e^{- y},\\qquad 2 x - 3>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{2 x - 3}\\cdot 2 \\\\ &=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}2 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{2}{2 x - 3} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{2}{e^{\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{2 x - 3} &=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(2 x - 3 \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{2 x - 3}.$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fef22b4-1658-51c4-9d88-3a9f9308339c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577186} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea23ce8-56d6-5036-b822-761465ad590a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fef22b4-1658-51c4-9d88-3a9f9308339c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577186} :answer-field/id #uuid "096de02a-e114-565a-97e3-fbb6d888f0b9" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20a047d6-d21d-54fd-bd52-edd9989ba98c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577187} {:answer/id #uuid "6c090d77-8107-5ce4-844f-f3f7a0f9ce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c090d77-8107-5ce4-844f-f3f7a0f9ce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577205} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd93e2fe-3095-5286-9d73-03800c413ede" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{1}{2 x}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b443023-21e5-58dc-940b-af2ebf834ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577190} {:answer/id #uuid "de6723ce-80d6-57fe-8de5-5cb46fe33516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b443023-21e5-58dc-940b-af2ebf834ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577190} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5208678-d293-56eb-9202-f5253a4e87ee" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577223}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "77fe441e-45a2-5d51-93a8-f4ea8416fd0f" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=4 e^{- y},\\qquad 4 x>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{1}{2 x}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4 x}\\cdot 4 \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{1}{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{1}{x}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}4 e^{- y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4}{e^{\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x} &=\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=\\ln{\\left(4 x \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc87408-521e-5ff3-81ad-d12b8336cba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577198} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5cc371-1e31-5af0-b590-b0e123a69dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #