577275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a265d0d-ea0d-51d2-a212-2a4111ec6a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577261} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5666fa9-c3aa-5e43-b2c8-bbc511366f41" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "729ec480-d7e2-58dc-a850-b9ff69610ca0" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{4 y}{x},\\qquad x\\ne 0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 x^{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- 8 x^{3}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 x^{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot 4 x^{3} \\\\ &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=- 2 x^{4}$ and $y\\prime=- 8 x^{3}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4 y}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &\\overset{?}{=}\\frac{4\\left(- 2 x^{4}\\right)}{x} \\\\ - 8 x^{3} &=- 8 x^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=- 2 x^{4}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=- 8 x^{3}.$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc0976d-8848-5bc7-a8ba-c6fb66573dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577288} {:answer/id #uuid "91cca939-abfa-579c-ba0f-76aed088ff08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cca939-abfa-579c-ba0f-76aed088ff08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577306} :answer-field/id #uuid "9baa3746-90cb-500b-8251-3017a1530a1d" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577312} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbb8d0f-0fc7-5f97-8c4c-958d8e7cec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577317} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7030f3-f3be-5e06-ba36-6216c88dadef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acbb8d0f-0fc7-5f97-8c4c-958d8e7cec21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577317} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4198222-2cf0-53fa-a803-9c2fa7bab7c3" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "112c328d-2c2a-5fc0-b7ee-7c0fdc2ad74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577283} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4cc2d0-e201-5801-b07a-6b913c46b3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa4cc2d0-e201-5801-b07a-6b913c46b3ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577316} :answer-field/id #uuid "e49426b3-4b2b-5454-8130-574f46902c18" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "57edc055-3dc9-5acb-8736-c0c617f4d5fc" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}},\\qquad 3 x + 2>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=- \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=-2\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=- \\frac{6}{3 x + 2}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}- 4 e^{\\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-(- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)})/(-2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\overset{?}{=}-4e^{-\\ln(3 x + 2)} \\\\ - \\frac{6}{3 x + 2} &\\not\\equiv - \\frac{4}{3 x + 2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=- 2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 2 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac82169-4017-5aee-b8a2-b79e679b0722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577295} {:answer/id #uuid "ee1fbee2-4889-5e84-9f46-037cf43d3d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ac82169-4017-5aee-b8a2-b79e679b0722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577295} :answer-field/id #uuid "4712b020-9702-5c3c-a3ff-cabe5f1d6dfc" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577291} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d576c80-7571-50d0-bc26-368ad4cb8fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577286} {:answer/id #uuid "42fb3203-d6f2-5685-9a07-82e33c2e8163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42fb3203-d6f2-5685-9a07-82e33c2e8163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577289} :answer-field/id #uuid "61085ad0-ae6c-5fc4-974f-fb93aeef646c" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ad3c8a-d899-5f30-9f69-f2953849fa2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577309} {:answer/id #uuid "9abd5e60-f344-53f9-9b87-6cfd5386e6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99ad3c8a-d899-5f30-9f69-f2953849fa2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577309} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a3ad4a5-9e8c-538b-8578-c03c5ca4643c" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "a098865b-a0f4-5d9b-a304-bd75a306b510" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=6 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}},\\qquad 4 x + 4>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=3\\cdot\\frac{4}{4 x + 4} \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false. Substituting $y=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}$ into the original equation gives expressions that are not identical:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}6 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{12}{4 x + 4} &\\overset{?}{=}6e^{-(3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)})/(3)} \\\\ \\frac{12}{4 x + 4} &\\overset{?}{=}6e^{-\\ln(4 x + 4)} \\\\ \\frac{12}{4 x + 4} &\\not\\equiv \\frac{3}{2 \\left(x + 1\\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is false. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is false, the function $y=3 \\ln{\\left(4 x + 4 \\right)}$ is not a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{4 x + 4}.$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06be9c0a-0223-57ac-aa2a-f18ff8de1f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577280} {:answer/id #uuid "6d228363-cf1a-5ff6-9768-677aa5961cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d228363-cf1a-5ff6-9768-677aa5961cc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577300} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d72eff3-71f9-5ab8-bb2e-d070834ba15b" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "182d1adb-f26c-5500-ab80-039d7a4be356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577285} {:answer/id #uuid "366b6039-d11a-5792-9c44-29c7e0c34e1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "182d1adb-f26c-5500-ab80-039d7a4be356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577285} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad95109-0cc0-5d78-83ab-75d8e54829d8" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{8}{4 x - 1}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577305} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76d2274a-f13b-5662-81b5-9656c55f0c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577302} {:answer/id #uuid "7a30a52a-1fcc-5a3c-9848-64fc5a681c65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76d2274a-f13b-5662-81b5-9656c55f0c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577302} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f3d032-bbe2-53bc-8f58-067bf98bacb8" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cb9ae8f4-b827-5abd-a900-f65d110847aa" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=8 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}},\\qquad 4 x - 1>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 1 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{8}{4 x - 1}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 1 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 1 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=2\\cdot\\frac{4}{4 x - 1} \\\\ &=\\frac{8}{4 x - 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 1 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{8}{4 x - 1}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}8 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{4 x - 1} &\\overset{?}{=}8e^{-(2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 1 \\right)})/(2)} \\\\ \\frac{8}{4 x - 1} &\\overset{?}{=}8e^{-\\ln(4 x - 1)} \\\\ \\frac{8}{4 x - 1} &=\\frac{8}{4 x - 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(4 x - 1 \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{8}{4 x - 1}.$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68427cdb-4aa1-5bed-8af1-4c431730eaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577299} {:answer/id #uuid "db9b80df-b1a1-5f03-abb8-805c0384bf6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db9b80df-b1a1-5f03-abb8-805c0384bf6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577321} :answer-field/id #uuid "6452302d-8c93-54b4-bd74-909afc8a339a" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d20a70-a6e3-569b-b70c-91a2deeda071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577282} {:answer/id #uuid "5f954ee0-b77e-54d7-9d1a-aeab4c66066f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d20a70-a6e3-569b-b70c-91a2deeda071" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577282} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c50a45c-a4d9-5db9-94cb-598f6ea148d1" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{3 x - 3}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13d2d4d3-772d-5fea-ab1e-f5d3a2ca4c1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577284} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb92550-d578-5696-a651-e77116f131ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdb92550-d578-5696-a651-e77116f131ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577329} :answer-field/id #uuid "be5959c5-b6f6-521b-a0a7-8f8644029a7d" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577319}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e4dd22fb-4eb9-516a-a3b0-458ee206af3b" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=9 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}},\\qquad 3 x - 3>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 3 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{12}{3 x - 3}.$ is false. Differentiating $f(x)=3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 3 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 3 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=3\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x - 3} \\\\ &=\\frac{9}{3 x - 3} \\\\ &\\not\\equiv \\frac{12}{3 x - 3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 3 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{9}{3 x - 3}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}9 e^{- \\frac{y}{3}} \\\\ \\frac{9}{3 x - 3} &\\overset{?}{=}9e^{-(3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 3 \\right)})/(3)} \\\\ \\frac{9}{3 x - 3} &\\overset{?}{=}9e^{-\\ln(3 x - 3)} \\\\ \\frac{9}{3 x - 3} &=\\frac{3}{x - 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=3 \\ln{\\left(3 x - 3 \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186577326 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93dc776f-23bf-56b1-9eee-5c4b2ad306a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577307} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcddebf-600d-5970-aedf-462499d377cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93dc776f-23bf-56b1-9eee-5c4b2ad306a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577307} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ade0d2-ac27-5c73-9ad6-3be99c3f833b" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08b1207b-6b24-5b40-bff6-3ccd28f9b09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577281} {:answer/id #uuid "97e3f8cb-3337-54fd-b5b1-647afcd593e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08b1207b-6b24-5b40-bff6-3ccd28f9b09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577281} :answer-field/id #uuid "51558782-e603-5130-857e-3b7d5a1aea98" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577292} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3b54604-0657-55bd-93ff-29802c0d79a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577314} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b137d2-ab8b-583a-a33b-00f008bb4c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6b137d2-ab8b-583a-a33b-00f008bb4c76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577328} :answer-field/id #uuid "54de8a04-1471-5f5a-8ae7-f7320ab59390" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{6}{3 x + 1}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186577293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ea016ba9-b08a-5130-a64c-616daed418ef" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\ny\\prime=6 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}},\\qquad 3 x + 1>0\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 1 \\right)}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in an interval where the function is defined and the equation is valid.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{6}{3 x + 1}.$ is true. Differentiating $f(x)=2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 1 \\right)},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\prime(x)&=\\left(2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 1 \\right)}\\right)\\prime \\\\ &=2\\cdot\\frac{3}{3 x + 1} \\\\ &=\\frac{6}{3 x + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true. Substituting $y=2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 1 \\right)}$ and $y\\prime=\\frac{6}{3 x + 1}$ into the original equation gives an identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\prime &\\overset{?}{=}6 e^{- \\frac{y}{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{3 x + 1} &\\overset{?}{=}6e^{-(2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 1 \\right)})/(2)} \\\\ \\frac{6}{3 x + 1} &\\overset{?}{=}6e^{-\\ln(3 x + 1)} \\\\ \\frac{6}{3 x + 1} &=\\frac{6}{3 x + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation” is true. Since statement “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement” is true, the function $y=2 \\ln{\\left(3 x + 1 \\right)}$ is a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f\\prime(x)=\\frac{6}{3 x + 1}.$; “Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true statement”; “The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation”."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693335 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77679ed5-30ad-58a4-a67e-d008a692077a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693343} {:answer/id #uuid "9e609747-80b4-5742-b33a-ed7c8093f92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e609747-80b4-5742-b33a-ed7c8093f92d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693348} :answer-field/id #uuid "2684c08f-56c6-5bfb-aae1-ae856adc7228" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true equality for every $x>0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0158c8c7-064d-5991-ab88-cfdc3ffbaf09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693329} {:answer/id #uuid "8af162c6-4d8b-54b4-92fc-9196afc61096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0158c8c7-064d-5991-ab88-cfdc3ffbaf09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693329} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2fa35a9-ab96-52d2-b2a3-70b17aad8650" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693353} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f76f58e-e96d-5849-a111-1be413d98dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693338} {:answer/id #uuid "53a40536-1066-5a5a-a749-0cf5dff276a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53a40536-1066-5a5a-a749-0cf5dff276a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693339} :answer-field/id #uuid "df05d84a-d4fa-5ec5-af3e-538b82a04555" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation on $(0,\\infty)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3731fce8-2fda-5013-b83b-ab216ad70ca1" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\nxe^y y\\prime-e^y=2x^2,\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=2\\ln x+\\ln 2$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The candidate is defined and differentiable for every $x>0$. Differentiating gives\n\n$$\nf\\prime(x)=\\frac{2}{x}+0=\\frac{2}{x}.\n$$\n\nThus the derivative statement is true. To substitute into the original equation, also simplify the exponential of the proposed function:\n\n$$\ne^{f(x)}=e^{2\\ln x+\\ln 2}=e^{2\\ln x}e^{\\ln 2}=2x^2.\n$$\n\nNow evaluate the entire left side, including both occurrences of $e^y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nxe^{f(x)}f\\prime(x)-e^{f(x)}\n&=x(2x^2)\\frac{2}{x}-2x^2\\\\\n&=4x^2-2x^2\\\\\n&=2x^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equals the right side for every $x>0$, so the substitution and solution statements are true as well. Equivalently, dividing the original equation by $xe^y$ gives $y\\prime=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2x}{e^y}$; substitution gives $\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{2}{x}$.\n\nSelect all three statements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d35811-e178-5f0d-a734-4510fb724bf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693344} {:answer/id #uuid "96dd28a0-049a-5ec6-b953-305403e0ea66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96dd28a0-049a-5ec6-b953-305403e0ea66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693347} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd78c32-d666-5b9b-a43b-52ec5cadbbf0" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true equality for every $x>0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc563f0-3c31-5618-8abb-72cd9d516aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693331} {:answer/id #uuid "b333b505-0fa8-5053-844d-365164da5482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b333b505-0fa8-5053-844d-365164da5482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693350} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7730f76-6d69-5428-a6bb-32b78bc361aa" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation on $(0,\\infty)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023f81d9-e807-56e7-82b7-f434973d05b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693330} {:answer/id #uuid "e97eeefd-696e-592c-9d86-ce0538885ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e97eeefd-696e-592c-9d86-ce0538885ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693357} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6cd2543-7b39-5b9a-971d-3624cb1fc22c" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=3x^2$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4c46d18e-0179-5dd7-a447-c88edeeac853" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny\\prime=\\frac{2y}{x},\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=x^3$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A solution must satisfy the differential equation at every point of the stated interval.\n\nFirst, differentiate:\n\n$$\nf\\prime(x)=3x^2.\n$$\n\nThe derivative statement is true. Now substitute the function and its actual derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf\\prime(x)&=3x^2,\\\\\n\\frac{2f(x)}{x}&=\\frac{2x^3}{x}=2x^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x>0$, these expressions are unequal because their difference is $x^2>0$. The substitution statement is false, so $y=f(x)$ is not a solution on $(0,\\infty)$. A correct derivative alone does not make a function a solution.\n\nSelect only the derivative statement."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693358 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dbe8507-2acc-56ba-8d1a-8d2ec68625b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693336} {:answer/id #uuid "94ee2bd4-3403-5e52-816f-cc0c12de6ae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dbe8507-2acc-56ba-8d1a-8d2ec68625b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693336} :answer-field/id #uuid "32bf7cfe-41e0-5972-a3b5-9515b006162f" :answer-field/key "Substituting $y=f(x)$ and $y\\prime=f\\prime(x)$ into the differential equation gives a true equality for every $x>0$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67243e27-10f4-57b1-ace8-f822e4cf4be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693341} {:answer/id #uuid "a40d5661-c14d-52d1-ad00-8ecd43e0f72b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67243e27-10f4-57b1-ace8-f822e4cf4be8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693341} :answer-field/id #uuid "65ffdaa4-3ba1-5adc-b231-2c7839383055" :answer-field/key "$f\\prime(x)=-xe^{-x^2}$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e85b95b-1f78-5568-a4bd-13ab3149288a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693342} {:answer/id #uuid "e335c2be-36a5-5065-989d-4bf57516071c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e85b95b-1f78-5568-a4bd-13ab3149288a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693342} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce0430f1-10ec-5fbf-9071-5a61942f76e8" :answer-field/key "The function $y=f(x)$ is a solution of the differential equation on $(0,\\infty)$." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f6090809-33ff-5c55-a7b0-d65b2137fd2a" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny\\prime=-2xy,\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)=e^{-x^2}$. Which statements are true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the proposed function using the chain rule:\n\n$$\nf\\prime(x)=e^{-x^2}\\frac{d}{dx}(-x^2)=-2xe^{-x^2}.\n$$\n\nThe derivative statement is false: the inner derivative is $-2x$, not $-x$.\n\nUse the actual derivative when checking the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf\\prime(x)&=-2xe^{-x^2},\\\\\n-2xf(x)&=-2xe^{-x^2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree for every $x>0$, so the substitution statement is true and $y=f(x)$ is a solution on $(0,\\infty)$. A false proposed derivative statement does not prevent the function itself from being a solution.\n\nSelect the substitution and solution statements."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693362 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09067945-8e8d-5988-9f4e-7e1a457619c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693359} {:answer/id #uuid "40dafaa6-52ae-5850-b05e-dad9231b2f83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{2(x-1)}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693365} {:answer/id #uuid "91cadaf3-ac2a-504f-958e-ff60048b7adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{2(x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693368} {:answer/id #uuid "a4950a5b-0431-5a2c-913e-5007b9802a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{-2(x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693373} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ccd092-8ada-5d19-98f3-b647c7f1bdda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91cadaf3-ac2a-504f-958e-ff60048b7adf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{2(x-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693368} :answer-field/id #uuid "20d97dfc-2668-5817-bd9f-4850c775c222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "210234e6-71a1-5eaf-9074-828fe418c108" :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=2y,\\qquad y(1)=3.\n$$\n\nWhich function is a solution to this initial value problem for all real $x$?" :question/worked-solution "A solution must satisfy both $f'(x)=2f(x)$ for every real $x$ and $f(1)=3$. Checking only one condition is insufficient.\n\nFor $f(x)=3e^{2(x-1)}$, the chain rule gives\n\n$$\nf'(x)=6e^{2(x-1)}=2f(x),\\qquad f(1)=3e^0=3.\n$$\n\nThis function passes both checks. Check the alternatives:\n\n- $f(x)=3e^{2x}$ satisfies $f'=2f$, but $f(1)=3e^2\\ne3$.\n- $f(x)=3e^{x-1}$ has $f(1)=3$, but $f'(x)=3e^{x-1}\\ne6e^{x-1}=2f(x)$.\n- $f(x)=2e^{2(x-1)}+1$ has $f(1)=3$, but $f'(x)=4e^{2(x-1)}$, while $2f(x)=4e^{2(x-1)}+2$.\n- $f(x)=3e^{-2(x-1)}$ has $f(1)=3$, but $f'(x)=-6e^{-2(x-1)}\\ne6e^{-2(x-1)}=2f(x)$.\n\nTherefore the solution is $y=3e^{2(x-1)}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1947e312-e8fd-527c-ad23-d3841ed3156e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693360} {:answer/id #uuid "85c69df4-6b46-5c34-a2e8-49232cf9abc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2/x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693367} {:answer/id #uuid "92b900aa-6e27-5145-a1c9-83eb88f52863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1/x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693369} {:answer/id #uuid "9717a56e-2f1c-569a-85d9-6077d02c3b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693371} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbc0061-4127-575c-b8a8-41362e5cd365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bbc0061-4127-575c-b8a8-41362e5cd365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2/x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693372} :answer-field/id #uuid "280e0883-bea0-554f-bc06-840eebd07b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3243f9ae-2514-5120-b619-d2b5c1f8463b" :question/problem "Consider the initial value problem on $x>0$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{y}{x},\\qquad y(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nThe derivatives of five candidate functions are supplied below.\n\n| Candidate $f(x)$ | Derivative $f'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-x/2$ | $-1/2$ |\n| $-1/x$ | $1/x^2$ |\n| $-2/x$ | $2/x^2$ |\n| $2/x$ | $-2/x^2$ |\n| $-2/x+1$ | $2/x^2$ |\n\nWhich function satisfies both the differential equation throughout $x>0$ and the initial condition?" :question/worked-solution "A solution must pass two checks: $f'(x)=-f(x)/x$ throughout $x>0$, and $f(2)=-1$.\n\nFor the candidates $-1/x$, $-2/x$, and $2/x$, substituting each function into $-f(x)/x$ gives its listed derivative. Their values at $x=2$ are, respectively, $-1/2$, $-1$, and $1$. Only $-2/x$ passes the initial-condition check.\n\nThe candidate $-x/2$ passes the initial condition, but fails the differential equation: its derivative is $-1/2$, whereas $-f(x)/x=1/2$.\n\nFor $f(x)=-2/x+1$, we have $f(2)=0$ and\n\n$$\n-\\frac{f(x)}{x}=\\frac{2}{x^2}-\\frac{1}{x}\\ne\\frac{2}{x^2}=f'(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore the solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{2}{x},\\qquad x>0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b97bf1-41e1-533b-bfb5-e685c31a7615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51b97bf1-41e1-533b-bfb5-e685c31a7615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693366} :answer-field/id #uuid "9324fc42-c714-5352-ac63-331b53679321" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c285e6e2-f853-5e31-8ad4-d4dec665aceb" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem on $x<0$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3y}{x},\\qquad y(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nYou are given that the solution has the form $y=Ax^3$. What is the value of the constant $A$?\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The given family already satisfies the differential equation. Choose its constant so that it also satisfies $y(-1)=3$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3&=A(-1)^3\\\\\n3&=-A\\\\\nA&=-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the solution is $y=-3x^3$ on $x<0$. Substituting $x=-1$ gives $y=3$, as required."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693380 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98211205-1aa8-55e3-b2f5-f87271895fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693392} {:answer/id #uuid "9e477bb5-80db-5153-803c-e3c4cada43b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98211205-1aa8-55e3-b2f5-f87271895fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693392} :answer-field/id #uuid "12ae57fc-150b-52d1-957f-2096750f4b5f" :answer-field/key "$y=\\ln(x^2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e2840b0-2ac0-5ae8-804f-97ef972ed53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693386} {:answer/id #uuid "d9f3a520-0bad-5a35-90a8-5360dbd6a975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e2840b0-2ac0-5ae8-804f-97ef972ed53d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693386} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a202c07-b1ff-5972-b362-9163ecc6dc25" :answer-field/key "$y=2\\ln(x+1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "033c7d7d-7eec-547d-8ebc-556dfe734ebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693377} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba06573-6d62-5c5c-ac3c-f9b02a0a224e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ba06573-6d62-5c5c-ac3c-f9b02a0a224e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693382} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7968bf-198b-5dcf-bc1a-cfd9606dcc3e" :answer-field/key "$y=\\ln(x^2+1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2874c788-59d1-5a94-a86e-6f00e6fd64f8" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2}{e^{y/2}},\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following functions are solutions on the entire interval $x>0$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A candidate is a solution if its derivative equals the right-hand side of the differential equation for every $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nFor $y=\\ln(x^2+1)$, differentiation and substitution give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'&=\\frac{2x}{x^2+1},\\\\\n\\frac{2}{e^{y/2}}&=\\frac{2}{e^{\\ln(x^2+1)/2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf these expressions were equal, multiplying by $(x^2+1)/2$ would give $x=\\sqrt{x^2+1}$. Squaring would give $x^2=x^2+1$, which is impossible. This function is not a solution.\n\nFor $y=2\\ln(x+1)$, the chain rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'&=\\frac{2}{x+1},\\\\\n\\frac{2}{e^{y/2}}&=\\frac{2}{e^{\\ln(x+1)}}=\\frac{2}{x+1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth sides agree for every $x>0$, so this function is a solution.\n\nFor $y=\\ln(x^2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'&=\\frac{2x}{x^2}=\\frac{2}{x},\\\\\n\\frac{2}{e^{y/2}}&=\\frac{2}{e^{\\ln(x^2)/2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x^2}}=\\frac{2}{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere $\\sqrt{x^2}=x$ because the stated interval has $x>0$. Both sides agree throughout the interval, so this function is a solution.\n\nSelect $y=2\\ln(x+1)$ and $y=\\ln(x^2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51322000-6dcb-5509-919c-11622e0b96e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693383} {:answer/id #uuid "f8c7fe5c-59b8-5e3c-b9fe-6929b91f6d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8c7fe5c-59b8-5e3c-b9fe-6929b91f6d77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693404} :answer-field/id #uuid "5898da25-fddb-5c07-8bf6-040702115180" :answer-field/key "$y=-e^x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693384} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05064ab1-5479-5d5f-a6ff-9e6aba54b029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693378} {:answer/id #uuid "b8149cbc-a91d-509c-9af4-34acc69ae081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8149cbc-a91d-509c-9af4-34acc69ae081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693396} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb3344c1-a723-5d40-8d52-f2b1c24972dc" :answer-field/key "$y=e^{-x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693399} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab5d01b6-142a-53b6-a66d-c45fd006e535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693394} {:answer/id #uuid "cf334ef4-00ae-5a50-8779-bf1fb6d9407f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf334ef4-00ae-5a50-8779-bf1fb6d9407f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693400} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5895681-b95d-5da6-b733-10b39d1ea073" :answer-field/key "$y=3e^x+1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2dde9857-88fe-51c0-a919-b9922972a417" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=y,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nThe derivatives of the proposed functions are provided:\n\n- For $y=3e^x+1$, $y'=3e^x$.\n- For $y=-e^x$, $y'=-e^x$.\n- For $y=e^{-x}$, $y'=-e^{-x}$.\n\nSubstitute each function and its derivative into the equation. Which functions are solutions? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A candidate is a solution if its derivative equals the right-hand side of the differential equation for every $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nFor $y=3e^x+1$, the derivative is $3e^x$, while the right-hand side is $3e^x+1$. They differ by $1$, so this function is not a solution.\n\nFor $y=-e^x$, both sides are $-e^x$ for every real $x$:\n\n$$\ny'=-e^x=y.\n$$\n\nThis function is a solution.\n\nFor $y=e^{-x}$, the derivative is $-e^{-x}$, while the right-hand side is $e^{-x}$. Since $e^{-x}>0$, these expressions are never equal. This function is not a solution.\n\nSelect only $y=-e^x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "817028db-5f8f-5822-8dbe-68eee0ffeb8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693389} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca6360c-d6df-5022-90c5-6cc2259897fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ca6360c-d6df-5022-90c5-6cc2259897fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693390} :answer-field/id #uuid "02cfd8ce-54eb-5ae0-abe6-b886ef2f2f42" :answer-field/key "$y=x^2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c612b767-7ec0-5e80-af30-46ff350cc018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693398} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfffd23-603d-55ee-9501-cf45b55bfae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebfffd23-603d-55ee-9501-cf45b55bfae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693402} :answer-field/id #uuid "c497b5d5-c807-501f-ad98-5e29b90c6fb0" :answer-field/key "$y=2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "724e1d7f-e142-5f90-8d03-91ac35b7f8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693388} {:answer/id #uuid "affe9e46-1c2f-5001-9120-7592358d390b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "724e1d7f-e142-5f90-8d03-91ac35b7f8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fecf6457-f431-5c1d-b765-2370406e87f1" :answer-field/key "$y=x^2+2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "706fa898-fd94-5abd-969d-cdea113d148f" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2y}{x}-2,\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following functions are solutions on $x>0$? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A candidate is a solution if its derivative equals the right-hand side of the differential equation for every $x$ in the stated domain.\n\nDifferentiate each proposed function, then substitute that function for $y$ on the right-hand side.\n\nFor $y=x^2+2x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'&=2x+2,\\\\\n\\frac{2y}{x}-2&=\\frac{2(x^2+2x)}{x}-2\\\\\n&=2x+4-2\\\\\n&=2x+2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth sides agree for every $x>0$, so this function is a solution.\n\nFor $y=x^2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'&=2x,\\\\\n\\frac{2y}{x}-2&=\\frac{2x^2}{x}-2=2x-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expressions differ by $2$, so this function is not a solution.\n\nFor $y=2x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny'&=2,\\\\\n\\frac{2y}{x}-2&=\\frac{2(2x)}{x}-2=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth sides agree for every $x>0$, so this function is a solution.\n\nSelect $y=x^2+2x$ and $y=2x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693648 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a244620-b8ae-5b65-bcc1-fdf819c4cc74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693640} {:answer/id #uuid "8c895671-9892-527c-9fd8-de7cc1b40542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c895671-9892-527c-9fd8-de7cc1b40542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693675} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b674aeb-7d03-5b56-85eb-847cae9fc3d2" :answer-field/key "$y=2\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3bd8f60-e6fd-58fd-a8e7-2caeb160cc5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693687} {:answer/id #uuid "d80acf5e-27ff-5b59-901a-85920ac26fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693692}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3bd8f60-e6fd-58fd-a8e7-2caeb160cc5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693687} :answer-field/id #uuid "55825839-2b8b-50ad-82e0-7e582fc1358f" :answer-field/key "$y=2\\ln\\left(x + 2\\right)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693659} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7509778-51f8-56c9-93c7-ef52d7c47dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693680} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d06d35-1445-5f82-84d5-24c747459bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4d06d35-1445-5f82-84d5-24c747459bea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693685} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dbb0104-50c6-53b7-a46a-3ff4588c6005" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d0d3ff-6e7a-5f9a-a270-e068b4dfa07b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693646} {:answer/id #uuid "5f9726e7-3a4a-5df3-a418-77c931eda3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f9726e7-3a4a-5df3-a418-77c931eda3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693661} :answer-field/id #uuid "a31ba3e1-ec27-5a87-ac28-f9686c1058d2" :answer-field/key "$y=-\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2c688b94-4b1e-59a0-9eb7-4419f5b91907" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=\\frac{2}{e^{y/2}},\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nWhich functions are solutions throughout the stated interval? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is a **solution** if its derivative equals the differential equation's right-hand side at every point of the stated interval. Differentiate each candidate and substitute it for $y$.\n\nFor $y=2\\ln\\left(x + 2\\right)$:\n\nThe logarithm arguments are positive because $x>0$. Using the exponential and logarithm identities gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{2\\ln\\left(x + 2\\right)}{2}}&=x + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=\\frac{2}{x + 2}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{2}{e^{\\frac{2\\ln\\left(x + 2\\right)}{2}}}\\\\&=\\frac{2}{x + 2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=-\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)$:\n\nThe logarithm arguments are positive because $x>0$. Using the exponential and logarithm identities gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{-\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)}{2}}&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x + 3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=- \\frac{1}{x + 3}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{2}{e^{\\frac{-\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)}{2}}}\\\\&=2 \\sqrt{x + 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, $y'=- \\frac{1}{4}$ whereas $\\text{RHS}=4$. Thus they are not identical, so this function **is not a solution**.\n\nFor $y=2\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)$:\n\nThe logarithm arguments are positive because $x>0$. Using the exponential and logarithm identities gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}e^{\\frac{2\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)}{2}}&=x + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=\\frac{2}{x + 3}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{2}{e^{\\frac{2\\ln\\left(x + 3\\right)}{2}}}\\\\&=\\frac{2}{x + 3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nSelect the functions verified above; do not select **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693652 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d8e4957-aa0c-5aa1-80a3-4cc471c4fe7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693641} {:answer/id #uuid "c5adfe67-a800-5482-9bb3-5748c6847222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d8e4957-aa0c-5aa1-80a3-4cc471c4fe7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693641} :answer-field/id #uuid "3259fb27-4e1d-567a-94a1-d396525fa008" :answer-field/key "$y=2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693649} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ea3243-5b2a-54a8-af51-0bab7985e2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693651} {:answer/id #uuid "fa14b820-385b-50a5-89ea-f8ef8e978b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43ea3243-5b2a-54a8-af51-0bab7985e2e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693651} :answer-field/id #uuid "518c1b02-ab22-5b02-80db-ddd15496f31b" :answer-field/key "$y=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693653} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aceb2374-8cdf-5bff-aa9e-ce6c8fade703" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693682} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9e7e1b-5dfb-5e44-90a2-d5816b58159b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb9e7e1b-5dfb-5e44-90a2-d5816b58159b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693698} :answer-field/id #uuid "779b49f2-01ae-5360-b453-9978b8df636b" :answer-field/key "$y=3 - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693671} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5fdd5da-6dcc-5a58-9607-06ffddd4631c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693697} {:answer/id #uuid "f405054f-b156-5abd-892d-2b61a184874b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5fdd5da-6dcc-5a58-9607-06ffddd4631c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693697} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e9e50c0-e3d9-5516-a161-afffdcf7f18a" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "44e5db8c-47b1-5df0-af12-21bdf7d9a354" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=\\left(2 y - 2\\right) \\cot{\\left(2 x \\right)},\\qquad 0<x<\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\n$$\n\nWhich functions are solutions throughout the stated interval? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is a **solution** if its derivative equals the differential equation's right-hand side at every point of the stated interval. Differentiate each candidate and substitute it for $y$.\n\nUse $\\cot(2 x)=\\frac{\\cos(2 x)}{\\sin(2 x)}$ on the stated interval.\n\nFor $y=\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=2\\cdot \\left(\\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 1-1\\right)\\cot\\left(2 x\\right)\\\\&=2 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=2\\cdot \\left(2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 3-1\\right)\\cot\\left(2 x\\right)\\\\&=4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 4 \\cot{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$, $y'=2 \\sqrt{2}$ whereas $\\text{RHS}=2 \\sqrt{2} + 4$. Thus they are not identical, so this function **is not a solution**.\n\nFor $y=3 - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=- 4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=2\\cdot \\left(3 - 2 \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)}-1\\right)\\cot\\left(2 x\\right)\\\\&=- 4 \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + 4 \\cot{\\left(2 x \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=\\frac{\\pi}{8}$, $y'=- 2 \\sqrt{2}$ whereas $\\text{RHS}=4 - 2 \\sqrt{2}$. Thus they are not identical, so this function **is not a solution**.\n\nSelect the functions verified above; do not select **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693656 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa522509-07b1-5dbe-ab79-638b51e3c8bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693681} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd3c50f-0c32-5afc-9602-2f672d7d38fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfd3c50f-0c32-5afc-9602-2f672d7d38fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693691} :answer-field/id #uuid "394fb778-49f2-5f91-9784-5257dcaa4ff8" :answer-field/key "$y=1 + e^{- x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693650} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01069849-3e04-5d0e-8f1e-c3d3ea946939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693639} {:answer/id #uuid "60a4dcd8-8025-5c4f-bfc9-f356da556df9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01069849-3e04-5d0e-8f1e-c3d3ea946939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693639} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e4260bd-55b7-53ad-9b5c-111384fc5197" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c0548d-cac6-5819-8cc1-6a3acebda0ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693655} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f62cd1-71d9-50b5-9313-9eaa1c822968" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51c0548d-cac6-5819-8cc1-6a3acebda0ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693655} :answer-field/id #uuid "77e364d7-a785-5a01-95c5-90c539736aa0" :answer-field/key "$y=1 - e^{- x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "761b57fd-4da7-5529-a6c4-b22e958c8e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693669} {:answer/id #uuid "b650d876-e867-5245-bece-aeaeb9cb5bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "761b57fd-4da7-5529-a6c4-b22e958c8e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693669} :answer-field/id #uuid "af14e2ce-8859-59b6-9610-165bef61573b" :answer-field/key "$y=2 + 2 e^{- x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "527bf3a5-34bb-5aaa-a8f4-1da12dee51ab" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=1 - y,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nWhich functions are solutions throughout the stated interval? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is a **solution** if its derivative equals the differential equation's right-hand side at every point of the stated interval. Differentiate each candidate and substitute it for $y$.\n\nFor $y=1 + e^{- x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=- e^{- x}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=-1\\cdot \\left(1 + e^{- x}-1\\right)\\\\&=- e^{- x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=1 - e^{- x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=e^{- x}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=-1\\cdot \\left(1 - e^{- x}-1\\right)\\\\&=e^{- x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=2 + 2 e^{- x}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=- 2 e^{- x}\\\\\\text{RHS}&=-1\\cdot \\left(2 + 2 e^{- x}-1\\right)\\\\&=-1 - 2 e^{- x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, $y'=- \\frac{2}{e}$ whereas $\\text{RHS}=-1 - \\frac{2}{e}$. Thus they are not identical, so this function **is not a solution**.\n\nSelect the functions verified above; do not select **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693668 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53e76986-3937-58e2-8bff-c3013b5381e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693657} {:answer/id #uuid "ec155434-8953-5c1b-9adc-d874e94ac295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53e76986-3937-58e2-8bff-c3013b5381e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693657} :answer-field/id #uuid "61ba58ee-1514-5385-bddb-a8941389765a" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693664} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dfd1163-5fe0-5c14-a4e9-331d6a938704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693642} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab19999-b6d1-5074-8401-f16ad8578981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dfd1163-5fe0-5c14-a4e9-331d6a938704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693642} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a12dcc7-c561-5b5a-b0da-4f8aa6682941" :answer-field/key "$y=- 2 x - 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d55c978-4c60-57fa-a009-dbc2a79a4872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693644} {:answer/id #uuid "fb592c81-bdb8-5bfa-bf0c-66be4d5962d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d55c978-4c60-57fa-a009-dbc2a79a4872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693644} :answer-field/id #uuid "8802fc04-8a26-5a24-a914-b20a53faf6fc" :answer-field/key "$y=- x - 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693674} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63c15da4-a9d1-5a63-9172-36eedc54f163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693665} {:answer/id #uuid "9110d944-8007-5f6c-b134-be20646215ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63c15da4-a9d1-5a63-9172-36eedc54f163" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693665} :answer-field/id #uuid "e031d340-7e46-5c9f-b523-cde947bd725f" :answer-field/key "$y=3 x - 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "70d1b24c-1fe7-52cf-9a3c-646cd935cfb1" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=\\frac{y + 1}{x},\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nWhich functions are solutions throughout the stated interval? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is a **solution** if its derivative equals the differential equation's right-hand side at every point of the stated interval. Differentiate each candidate and substitute it for $y$.\n\nFor $y=- x - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=-1\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{1\\cdot \\left(- x - 1+1\\right)}{x}\\\\&=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=3 x - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=3\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{1\\cdot \\left(3 x - 1+1\\right)}{x}\\\\&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=- 2 x - 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=-2\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{1\\cdot \\left(- 2 x - 1+1\\right)}{x}\\\\&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nSelect the functions verified above; do not select **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693700 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ff0f086-33fa-5a74-917c-5f711016bc23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693662} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2a1b7d-8a2a-5c5f-99cd-aa463f3f0a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ff0f086-33fa-5a74-917c-5f711016bc23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693662} :answer-field/id #uuid "140a858f-4128-58d8-9a73-6aa085413817" :answer-field/key "$y=- x^{2} - 2 x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56978625-8c3a-5a32-bf58-92f401c0ffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693660} {:answer/id #uuid "ad5def5f-f612-5b3b-a093-4e8576ed22ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad5def5f-f612-5b3b-a093-4e8576ed22ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693683} :answer-field/id #uuid "220bb3ea-231b-57e7-98e1-6e143fd92ec6" :answer-field/key "$y=1 - 2 x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693645} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b6da22-b4d0-505f-90b5-ca050d127b61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693654} {:answer/id #uuid "dd69c6e7-8e40-59b4-867a-837e1d6e56e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd69c6e7-8e40-59b4-867a-837e1d6e56e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693694} :answer-field/id #uuid "dab9be17-fe6e-5f29-93f6-30d2173802ab" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55421c6d-650c-526d-9087-11b97033b4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693658} {:answer/id #uuid "766ed623-0fd6-5462-85ee-2d1c58bf2fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "766ed623-0fd6-5462-85ee-2d1c58bf2fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693670} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b157a1-bc0b-5fd7-bf7d-8fe8f62c6a0d" :answer-field/key "$y=x^{2} - 3 x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ee067844-2bda-5854-bc5b-b4e27fb39b5f" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\ny'=2 + \\frac{2 y}{x},\\qquad x>0.\n$$\n\nWhich functions are solutions throughout the stated interval? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is a **solution** if its derivative equals the differential equation's right-hand side at every point of the stated interval. Differentiate each candidate and substitute it for $y$.\n\nFor $y=1 - 2 x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=-2\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{2\\cdot \\left(1 - 2 x\\right)}{x}+2\\\\&=-2 + \\frac{2}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, $y'=-2$ whereas $\\text{RHS}=0$. Thus they are not identical, so this function **is not a solution**.\n\nFor $y=- x^{2} - 2 x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=- 2 x - 2\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{2\\cdot \\left(- x^{2} - 2 x\\right)}{x}+2\\\\&=- 2 x - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe two expressions agree throughout the interval, so this function **is a solution**.\n\nFor $y=x^{2} - 3 x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y'&=2 x - 3\\\\\\text{RHS}&=\\frac{2\\cdot \\left(x^{2} - 3 x\\right)}{x}+2\\\\&=2 x - 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=1$, $y'=-1$ whereas $\\text{RHS}=-2$. Thus they are not identical, so this function **is not a solution**.\n\nSelect the functions verified above; do not select **None of the above**."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693708 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5270db35-1f63-50fa-888e-06b62546fc3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693714} {:answer/id #uuid "d81d3e7a-e21e-5f13-927a-8f2a1b1e4372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693728}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5270db35-1f63-50fa-888e-06b62546fc3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.